"Agent cloaking" / differential serving to AI crawlers was demonstrated as a
proof-of-concept by SPLX (the "AI-targeted cloaking" Atlas demo) and studied in
"The Parallel-Poisoned Web" (arXiv:2509.00124). The wild indirect-prompt-injection
census (arXiv:2604.27202) measured injection at scale under a single user-agent.
agentview's contribution is the first prevalence measurement of *agent-directed
content divergence* — comparing the human view and the AI-crawler view of the same
URLs side by side.

Site rankings for the study seed list come from the Tranco list
(https://tranco-list.eu), Le Pochat et al., NDSS 2019.
